1
00:00:04,100 --> 00:00:10,371
Every shift, technicians walk plant rooms and basements to check equipment.

2
00:00:10,971 --> 00:00:14,264
Down there, the signal is often gone.

3
00:00:14,864 --> 00:00:22,398
Rounds brings AI to that inspection round, while approved rules keep the final say on safety.

4
00:00:23,998 --> 00:00:31,213
A supervisor starts with the equipment manual. This one is fictional, made for the demo.

5
00:00:31,813 --> 00:00:36,867
Firebase AI Logic sends it once to Gemini in the cloud.

6
00:00:37,467 --> 00:00:40,681
Gemini compiles it into a procedure pack:

7
00:00:40,681 --> 00:00:47,566
limits the app can enforce, and one small card per step for the on-device model.

8
00:00:49,166 --> 00:00:52,706
Every limit must quote the manual word for word,

9
00:00:52,706 --> 00:00:55,853
and the app checks each quote in code.

10
00:00:56,453 --> 00:01:03,651
Here, it flagged a safety line that Gemini reworded, so the supervisor excludes it.

11
00:01:04,251 --> 00:01:08,809
Nothing reaches technicians until every item is approved.

12
00:01:10,409 --> 00:01:16,392
The technician starts the round, and the approved pack is stored on the device.

13
00:01:16,992 --> 00:01:19,438
Now the connection drops.

14
00:01:20,038 --> 00:01:25,413
At the first check, the technician notes a faint rattling near the pump.

15
00:01:26,013 --> 00:01:32,313
Chrome's built-in Gemini Nano, called through the same Firebase AI Logic SDK,

16
00:01:32,313 --> 00:01:35,989
reviews the note on the device, offline.

17
00:01:37,589 --> 00:01:42,099
Next, an abnormal reading: eighty-two degrees.

18
00:01:42,699 --> 00:01:48,990
No AI judges this number. A rule compares it with the approved limit,

19
00:01:48,990 --> 00:01:54,313
quotes the manual, and shows the escalation rule the supervisor approved.

20
00:01:54,913 --> 00:01:59,088
It also sees that this check failed on an earlier shift.

21
00:02:00,688 --> 00:02:06,670
At the vibration check, the reading is high again, with a squeal near the bearing.

22
00:02:07,270 --> 00:02:12,828
For a deeper look, the technician sees exactly what would be sent,

23
00:02:12,828 --> 00:02:16,533
and agrees. Offline, it waits on the device.

24
00:02:17,133 --> 00:02:20,177
When the connection returns, the changes sync,

25
00:02:20,177 --> 00:02:26,699
and Gemini in the cloud reviews it with the manual section and this check's history.

26
00:02:28,299 --> 00:02:30,740
At the end of the round,

27
00:02:30,740 --> 00:02:36,842
the device drafts the shift handover, on top of facts taken from the recorded readings.

28
00:02:37,442 --> 00:02:40,530
Rounds. The cloud prepares the knowledge,

29
00:02:40,530 --> 00:02:46,192
the device helps offline, and approved rules decide what is safe.

